            <ArticleTitle>Non-Genetic Transmission of Obesity - It's in Your Epigenes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>349-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tem.2016.04.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1043-2760(16)30019-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity and its related metabolic comorbidities can be inherited across generations through non-genetic mechanisms. In a recent report, Huypens et al., using an in vitro fertilization approach, provide evidence that exposure to a high-fat diet modifies egg and sperm epigenetic information, rendering the progeny more prone to obesity.</AbstractText>
